# PUBLIC repo — LumosCore is open source. Ships built output (dist/) plus the build tooling
# (_tools/) and the Cloudflare Functions.
#
# The ADMIN PANEL IS NOT IN THIS REPO. dist-admin/ has its own separate PRIVATE repo, because the
# panel's protection is that its files are not on any public server — publishing them here would
# undo that. It is ignored below; do not remove that rule.

# --- admin panel: separate private repo -------------------------------------------------------
dist-admin/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Eight of these still contain the OLD Soroswap key. Committing them would put a secret in the git
# history permanently — deleting the file later does NOT remove it from history.
_tools/*.bak_*
*.bak
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars

# --- source containers (337 MB) --------------------------------------------------------------
# The design exports the transforms read from. Excluded to keep the repo small.
# NOTE: that means GitHub is a DEPLOYMENT mechanism here, not a backup of your source. Keep
# C:\LumosCore\_BACKUP_* (and ideally an off-machine copy) — the repo will not save you.
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Without it these patterns match at EVERY depth, which also excluded
# dist/lumoscore-*-mobile.html — the 16 built mobile pages. They were never committed, so the deployed
# site had no mobile pages at all and every phone visitor got a 404 on every route. The middleware
# rewrites a mobile request to lumoscore-<page>-mobile, and that file simply was not on the server.
# Anchor these to the repo root so they only exclude the source containers they were written for.
/lumoscore-*-desktop.html
/lumoscore-*-mobile.html

# --- local build/run artefacts ---------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.wrangler/
.mf/
npm-debug.log*
*.log

# --- source asset library (137 MB) -----------------------------------------------------------
# dist/assets already holds every image, video and logo the built site actually references, and it
# is what Cloudflare serves. This root folder is the wider source library and is not needed to
# deploy. Same caveat as above: keep your own backup of it.
/assets/*
# ...except the token logos. They are 264 KB against 138 MB for the rest, and unlike the wider library
# they are NOT reproducible: each one is a token's X profile picture fetched once by _tools/_launchicons.js.
# dist/ alone is not enough to keep them -- extract_site.js copies assets/ INTO dist/, so a rebuild on a
# clone without this folder would quietly delete every logo from the deploy. That is the container-drift
# failure this project has hit before, and tracking these few files is what closes it.
!/assets/tokens/
# ...and the Trade hero gradients, for the same reason: authored here, not downloadable again.
!/assets/hero/

# --- backups and scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# broad on purpose — several backup folders here do not share one prefix
*BACKUP*/
*_LOCK_*/
_FINAL_*/
_MAINNET_MIGRATION_*/
_scrap/
dist/_scrap/

# --- OS noise --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
